ued in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full in ","type":"text"},{"code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" §2.1. The short version: deny-override buys one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checkable property — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adding a deny rule can never widen access, and can never be undone by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding allows","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — and most-specific-wins buys expressiveness at the cost of making “is X","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied?” unanswerable without enumerating every other rule that might out-specify it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"PermissionEffect::Allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] is the default, so data written before this existed, and clients","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that send no ","type":"text"},{"code":"effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", both mean “allow”. No migration.","type":"text"}]}}}